diff --git a/docs/state-sync.md b/docs/state-sync.md
index 40fcdcd4..51037584 100644
--- a/docs/state-sync.md
+++ b/docs/state-sync.md
@@ -1112,3 +1112,12 @@ gets a shrunk test before its fix. The comparison with master, and every model r
   `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-15-difference-too-long-design.md` (the differenceTooLong rules).
 - `docs/superpowers/plans/`: the stage plans, kept as history.
 - `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-14-state-sync-foundation/followups.md`: what each stage parked.
+
+
+## MoonGram: explicit outgoing read suppression
+
+MoonGram adds opt-in per-account device-local settings in MoonGramCore. This is a deliberate exception for outgoing cloud read receipts only, not an exception to history/update/difference retry rules. `synchronizePeerReadState` confirms both pending Push and Validate operations using the existing `confirmSynchronized` helper when suppression is enabled, leaving local read markers/counts intact. Secret-chat read synchronization is unchanged. Thread reads and local mention/reaction/content cleanup are retained while their selected outgoing RPCs are omitted. Operation-log workers still remove completed entries. No fake pts/affected-message result is injected.
+
+The portable regression probe compiles the actual privacy helper and top-level read gate against Telegram's real Signal/Subscriber/Disposable/Atomic/mapping code, with Postbox/store/network stand-ins. It checks live policy updates, account routing, observer disposal, subscription-time decisions and queue confirmation for Push/Validate. This is not an actual Postbox/network integration test or the state-sync truth-server seed suite. Full client and two-account/device verification remain required.
+
+A receipt already sent cannot be recalled; other sessions remain independent. Disabling suppression resumes cumulative read bounds, which can acknowledge older locally-read messages. Privacy settings are separate from cosmetic enable/display mode and are never exported in the shared profile.
